      "writtenOn": "2015-06-10T22:14:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The search for 0xea starts at the end of the image and goes backwards i.e. at an offset of 96*1024 (CONFIG_FW_IMAGE_SIZE) bytes from the start of the image.  It does not start from the end of the partition such that we would get into reading the CRC+tag. So I think we are good there. We are only skipping the padded 0xFFs.\n\nThe execution time is roughly 52 milliseconds.",
